at d14b06726cabab09c68a403ce2e684a52efbfe4c.

No source file from it is vendored. The generator in its src/relief.rs,
src/field.rs, src/distance.rs and src/color.rs is ported, step for step, to the
GLSL passes in platform/render/relief_glsl.h. The port runs on the GPU every
frame, because the game's art only exists once the ROM has been decoded into
VRAM; the crate's PNG/GIF front end and its CLI and wasm wrappers are not used.

Where the port differs from the crate:

- The distance to the silhouette is capped instead of unbounded: at 32 px
  for sprites, which no GBA sprite (64x64 at most) reaches, so they are exact;
  at 12 px for background layers, whose solid ground would otherwise become
  one dome the size of the room.
- Islands (8-connected components) are not split out. The crate processes
  them one at a time, but that only re-centres the lightness, and its
  normalised blur makes that a no-op.
- Intermediates are half floats.
- Background layers use the crate's defaults: normal strength 1.5, detail
  strength 6, detail scale 0.6, shape strength 1.15, shape radius 4, softness
  1.15, alpha threshold 0.03, OpenGL green channel.  Sprites use detail
  strength 2 (the CLI's --detail-strength 2): the game's sprites are shaded
  already, and at 6 lighting that shading again doubled it.
- Sprites are processed per group of touching hardware sprites (one
  character), not per hardware sprite.
